WEBVTT

00:01:24.680 --> 00:01:27.440
<i>Marie falls victim to a fatal
case of tropical fever.</i>

00:01:27.440 --> 00:01:32.150
<i>Nadia pleads with Captain Nemo
to save Marie, but he refuses.</i>

00:01:32.150 --> 00:01:36.030
<i>Nadia asks which is more important,
to commit murder or to save a life?</i>

00:01:36.030 --> 00:01:38.530
<i>During her entreaties, Nadia also
falls victim to tropical fever.</i>

00:01:38.530 --> 00:01:41.200
<i>The two girls hover between
life and death.</i>

00:01:41.200 --> 00:01:45.660
<i>The person who saves their lives is
none other than Captain Nemo.</i>

00:02:06.810 --> 00:02:09.270
Okay, ready to start.

00:02:09.270 --> 00:02:10.940
Hanson, press the switch.

00:02:11.110 --> 00:02:12.570
Okay!

00:02:18.660 --> 00:02:22.530
The heat-resistant super-alloy used in
the engine room is very durable.

00:02:22.530 --> 00:02:23.990
It won't melt even under this heat.

00:02:23.990 --> 00:02:28.000
We invented a metal cutter based on
the special properties of that metal,

00:02:28.000 --> 00:02:30.710
and the huge power supply on
this ship in only three days!

00:02:31.080 --> 00:02:33.960
That makes us geniuses!

00:02:33.960 --> 00:02:37.010
It was this ship that made it possible.

00:02:38.010 --> 00:02:40.510
How do you feel, Jean?

00:02:41.510 --> 00:02:42.600
Mr. Fait!

00:02:42.930 --> 00:02:44.350
Did it work out all right?

00:02:44.350 --> 00:02:49.770
Yes, it's all due to the heat resistant
material you gave us. Thanks!

00:02:49.770 --> 00:02:54.570
I'm glad to hear that. It was just
an extra piece lying around.

00:02:54.570 --> 00:02:58.990
I see. You sure have amazing
technology on this ship.

00:03:02.370 --> 00:03:03.200
Ouch!

00:03:07.500 --> 00:03:08.450
My mistake!

00:03:10.790 --> 00:03:13.000
Hurry, it'll burn a hole
through the Nautilus!

00:03:13.380 --> 00:03:14.840
Come on!

00:03:17.760 --> 00:03:19.340
Just in time!

00:03:20.800 --> 00:03:24.720
Oh, no! My glasses!
Where are my glasses?

00:03:26.220 --> 00:03:28.680
My glasses... my glasses...
my glasses!

00:03:28.680 --> 00:03:31.350
What's wrong? Why are
you on the floor?

00:03:41.280 --> 00:03:43.660
I'm sorry.

00:03:45.490 --> 00:03:51.370
These glasses are the only thing l
have that my father bought me.

00:03:51.960 --> 00:03:54.080
He was very seldom at home.

00:03:56.090 --> 00:03:57.670
I'm so sorry.

00:04:01.340 --> 00:04:06.600
Don't worry too much about it. I guess
it had to happen sooner or later.

00:04:06.600 --> 00:04:10.560
It's only God's way of telling me not to
get overly concerned about Dad.

00:04:12.940 --> 00:04:15.520
If anything breaks, you just fix it!

00:04:16.020 --> 00:04:19.940
Anything other than life
can be replaced.

00:04:19.940 --> 00:04:24.070
Spilt water can't be returned, but you
can always pour in some more.

00:04:25.280 --> 00:04:28.240
Give me those. I'll fix them for you.

00:04:28.240 --> 00:04:30.700
You can fix these onboard?!

00:04:31.040 --> 00:04:37.250
Yes, we have all kinds of facilities so
that we don't have to go ashore.

00:04:37.250 --> 00:04:39.710
It's unbelievable! You can't
beat technology!

00:04:39.880 --> 00:04:41.550
That's right.

00:04:44.590 --> 00:04:46.220
I can't agree with that.

00:04:50.520 --> 00:04:53.480
Unidentified ship at 2 o'clock.

00:04:54.100 --> 00:04:58.020
Shallow draught and slow speed.
Could be a whale.

00:04:58.690 --> 00:05:02.490
Could be, but it could also
be the Garfish.

00:05:03.360 --> 00:05:07.030
We can't tell at this distance.
Let's get closer.

00:05:07.030 --> 00:05:08.490
Roger.

00:05:08.950 --> 00:05:10.990
What? Fixed already?

00:05:12.410 --> 00:05:17.080
They're just like they were before.
Thanks, Mr. Fait!

00:05:17.330 --> 00:05:20.170
It's nothing, just another
victory for science.

00:05:20.170 --> 00:05:21.880
Oh, yeah!

00:05:21.880 --> 00:05:26.260
By the way, Jean, things don't seem
so smooth between you and Nadia.

00:05:26.260 --> 00:05:31.600
Give these to her. Women are always
pushovers for flowers.

00:05:31.600 --> 00:05:34.560
This is great! Where did you get these?

00:05:34.730 --> 00:05:39.110
Grew them on this ship, another
victory for science.

00:05:39.110 --> 00:05:41.820
Well, I've got to get back to
work. See you later.

00:05:41.820 --> 00:05:43.400
Right, until later!

00:05:43.400 --> 00:05:45.030
Be nice to her now.

00:05:47.200 --> 00:05:52.030
What an amazing ship! So
convenient! Right, Nadia?

00:05:52.030 --> 00:05:53.790
I guess so.

00:05:54.750 --> 00:05:55.790
What's the matter?

00:05:56.120 --> 00:05:58.420
Yes, it's convenient!

00:05:58.420 --> 00:06:01.750
So what? It only makes people lazier.

00:06:01.750 --> 00:06:04.380
That's not so. It can bring
happiness too.

00:06:05.300 --> 00:06:08.840
Here, for you. A present!

00:06:09.510 --> 00:06:12.930
Oh, how pretty they are!
Where did you get them?

00:06:13.680 --> 00:06:15.640
This ship made them for me.

00:06:20.190 --> 00:06:24.480
What's a convenient ship of science
good for? It's only a killing tool!

00:06:28.280 --> 00:06:32.830
Wait up! Hey, Nadia, what's wrong?

00:06:32.830 --> 00:06:37.790
It's not right! Flowers and trees should
not be man-made. It's wrong!

00:06:37.790 --> 00:06:40.460
It's no different from what
Gargoyle is doing!

00:06:40.460 --> 00:06:42.250
Is that so?

00:06:52.300 --> 00:06:53.890
What can this be?

00:06:55.810 --> 00:06:56.850
This plate...

00:06:57.100 --> 00:07:02.230
The Nautilus, launched June 21, 1888.

00:07:02.860 --> 00:07:06.730
Amazing! This is the nameplate
for the Nautilus!

00:07:06.730 --> 00:07:08.780
But I wonder what the strange
letters at the bottom mean?

00:07:09.450 --> 00:07:15.740
The Eritrium, launched into space,
sidereal calendar year 7962.

00:07:17.290 --> 00:07:18.870
You can read that?

00:07:19.870 --> 00:07:24.250
It's amazing that you can read it!
What hidden talents!

00:07:25.420 --> 00:07:27.050
I wonder why I was able to read it?

00:07:27.920 --> 00:07:31.010
I wonder what these letters
really mean?

00:07:31.010 --> 00:07:33.680
The name plate in the engine room?

00:07:34.100 --> 00:07:39.020
Yes, the one that has the launching
date of the Nautilus.

00:07:39.020 --> 00:07:41.020
Oh, you saw that.

00:07:41.020 --> 00:07:46.150
Please tell me what the plate beneath is.
It's not metal or stone.

00:07:46.150 --> 00:07:50.360
And those strange letters which say
"Eritrium". What do they mean?

00:07:50.700 --> 00:07:53.280
Jean, were you able to
read those letters?!

00:07:53.280 --> 00:07:56.160
No, not me. It was Nadia.

00:07:57.790 --> 00:07:59.250
I see. It was Nadia.

00:07:59.250 --> 00:08:01.210
Please tell me what they mean.

00:08:02.160 --> 00:08:07.460
Jean, human beings have this hunger
to find out what they don't know.

00:08:07.460 --> 00:08:09.800
Curiosity and a desire for
knowledge, right?

00:08:09.800 --> 00:08:11.420
That's right, but

00:08:11.420 --> 00:08:14.390
there are things in this world which we
are better off not knowing about.

00:08:15.930 --> 00:08:19.770
Yes, we are much happier not
knowing about such things.

00:08:28.570 --> 00:08:31.690
The unknown ship approaching us has
been identified as the Garfish.

00:08:42.870 --> 00:08:44.540
All hands to general quarters.

00:08:44.540 --> 00:08:48.250
All hands to general quarters.
Prepare for action against the enemy.

00:08:48.630 --> 00:08:49.670
It's general quarters!

00:08:50.460 --> 00:08:52.010
So it's war again.

00:08:52.010 --> 00:08:54.630
Say, Nadia, let's go
up to the bridge.

00:08:54.630 --> 00:08:57.510
But we're not supposed to
go there during battle.

00:08:57.510 --> 00:09:00.560
It'll be okay. We're just
going to take a peek.

00:09:00.560 --> 00:09:03.890
Besides, if you see the
Nautilus destroy the Garfish,

00:09:03.890 --> 00:09:05.980
you may learn to like this ship.

00:09:06.480 --> 00:09:07.940
Come on, let's go!

00:09:13.150 --> 00:09:15.110
How is the Garfish reacting?

00:09:15.110 --> 00:09:17.110
No change. Range, 5,000.

00:09:17.360 --> 00:09:20.200
Why doesn't it attack us
with torpedoes?

00:09:20.200 --> 00:09:22.080
Have they given up?

00:09:22.080 --> 00:09:25.410
The Nautilus' defense system
is too much for them.

00:09:25.410 --> 00:09:29.340
You'd have to have a whole fleet of
battleships to take on this ship.

00:09:37.720 --> 00:09:40.180
You shouldn't be here!
We're at battle stations.

00:09:40.180 --> 00:09:43.140
But we want to see the
Nautilus in operation.

00:09:43.140 --> 00:09:46.600
Go back to your room. This is not
a playground for children.

00:09:46.890 --> 00:09:47.770
But...

00:09:47.770 --> 00:09:50.310
Come on, Jean, let's go back.

00:09:52.110 --> 00:09:53.110
What was that?

00:10:02.160 --> 00:10:03.950
Something is striking against the hull.

00:10:04.290 --> 00:10:05.000
A trap, maybe?

00:10:12.840 --> 00:10:13.550
What's happening?!

00:10:14.090 --> 00:10:15.880
They've unleashed a new weapon!

00:10:15.880 --> 00:10:18.380
Our super electromagnetic engine's
magnetic field has become distorted.

00:10:21.390 --> 00:10:23.010
All engines have stopped!

00:10:23.010 --> 00:10:25.140
The power source for our scanning
system has been destroyed.

00:10:25.140 --> 00:10:27.350
The control wires to our fire control
system have been severed.

00:10:27.730 --> 00:10:29.350
The Nautilus is disabled.

00:10:32.480 --> 00:10:33.230
What's that?

00:10:36.740 --> 00:10:38.700
Torpedoes approaching from
the starboard side!

00:10:38.700 --> 00:10:41.410
I count four torpedoes. Distance based
on visual sighting, 4,000.

00:10:41.660 --> 00:10:42.740
The defensive system!

00:10:42.740 --> 00:10:43.740
Not working!

00:10:44.700 --> 00:10:45.740
What shall we do?!

00:10:45.740 --> 00:10:47.410
Let them come to within 800 meters.

00:10:47.410 --> 00:10:50.670
At that moment, fill the ballast tanks
and go into a vertical dive.

00:10:51.000 --> 00:10:51.630
Aye aye, Sir.

00:10:51.630 --> 00:10:53.170
Range 1200!

00:10:54.710 --> 00:10:56.460
Range 800!

00:10:56.460 --> 00:10:58.050
Fill the ballast tanks!

00:11:04.310 --> 00:11:05.680
They're still coming! Range 300!

00:11:11.810 --> 00:11:13.610
Three torpedoes passed
over and under us.

00:11:14.270 --> 00:11:16.070
The fourth one is coming now!

00:11:21.280 --> 00:11:23.160
It passed in front of the bridge.

00:11:24.530 --> 00:11:25.990
We're safe!

00:11:26.660 --> 00:11:28.000
Where is it now?

00:11:28.000 --> 00:11:30.410
I think it's at 9 o'clock.

00:11:30.960 --> 00:11:34.920
I found it! Garfish approaching
from the starboard side!

00:11:35.420 --> 00:11:36.880
It's headed for us at full speed!

00:11:37.250 --> 00:11:38.840
Do they intend to ram us?!

00:11:38.840 --> 00:11:40.220
Get us away, now!

00:11:43.050 --> 00:11:45.470
There's no response! It won't move!

00:11:45.470 --> 00:11:47.470
All personnel on the starboard side,
move immediately to the port side!

00:11:48.020 --> 00:11:49.770
All quarters prepare for impact!

00:11:50.230 --> 00:11:51.020
Here it comes!

00:12:05.200 --> 00:12:06.950
Amazing! We repulsed the Garfish!

00:12:19.510 --> 00:12:20.590
We beat them!

00:12:26.640 --> 00:12:29.850
Gosh, they sure are a reckless bunch!

00:12:29.850 --> 00:12:33.890
They were probably ordered
to make a suicide attack.

00:12:35.020 --> 00:12:36.310
How terrible!

00:12:37.480 --> 00:12:38.770
What are our damages?

00:12:39.070 --> 00:12:41.150
Damage to the number seven
starboard tank.

00:12:41.150 --> 00:12:43.360
Depth indicator is inoperable.

00:12:43.360 --> 00:12:45.450
Leakages on starboard side
have been stopped.

00:12:45.450 --> 00:12:47.200
All engine units are inoperable.

00:12:48.120 --> 00:12:52.450
We have to surface and
make external repairs.

00:12:53.210 --> 00:12:56.250
Purge water from all ballast tanks.
We're going to surface.

00:12:56.250 --> 00:12:56.920
Aye, aye!

00:13:15.390 --> 00:13:18.980
Found you at last! You sea monster!

00:13:20.480 --> 00:13:23.900
Ready cannons for firing!

00:13:24.280 --> 00:13:27.910
Target, the large submarine off
the starboard side!

00:13:30.620 --> 00:13:33.620
Now I'm going to pay you
back for the Abraham

00:13:33.620 --> 00:13:39.710
with my USS Barracuda and
the whole American Fleet!

00:13:49.050 --> 00:13:50.050
What is it?

00:13:50.470 --> 00:13:52.510
The Garfish is destroyed,
so why is it shining?

00:13:52.510 --> 00:13:54.980
American Fleet, off the starboard side!

00:14:05.900 --> 00:14:06.990
Missile salvo on the mark!

00:14:06.990 --> 00:14:09.490
Good! Fire the second salvo!

00:14:09.910 --> 00:14:11.910
Keep firing! Hit it with all we've got!

00:14:18.420 --> 00:14:20.880
Sink, you evil sea monster!

00:14:23.340 --> 00:14:26.800
Second salvo fired!
Arrival time fifty seconds!

00:14:26.800 --> 00:14:28.760
All quarters, prepare for
shelling defense!

00:14:28.760 --> 00:14:30.970
Close off all armored shutters!

00:14:34.970 --> 00:14:36.060
Emergency dive!

00:14:36.060 --> 00:14:38.690
We can't! The diving system
isn't working!

00:14:39.770 --> 00:14:40.560
Incoming!

00:14:47.360 --> 00:14:51.740
Well, it was a good thing we
listened to that fellow!

00:14:52.120 --> 00:14:54.200
You mean that guy in a mask?

00:14:54.620 --> 00:14:57.580
I don't care who's behind that mask!

00:14:58.290 --> 00:15:00.960
I just want revenge for
my men who died!

00:15:03.500 --> 00:15:05.460
Hit 'em! Hit 'em! Hit 'em!

00:15:05.750 --> 00:15:07.920
That's revenge for Jean and Nadia!

00:15:14.470 --> 00:15:16.390
Hits on starboard aft deck!

00:15:16.390 --> 00:15:17.980
Damage to second auxiliary engine!

00:15:17.980 --> 00:15:19.810
Direct hits on our diving fins!

00:15:19.810 --> 00:15:23.650
Purge all compressed air from number
one through thirty-two!

00:15:23.650 --> 00:15:26.320
But we'll lose our floating balance!

00:15:26.320 --> 00:15:29.030
It doesn't matter! Open all
emergency ports!

00:15:29.030 --> 00:15:29.990
Roger!

00:15:31.820 --> 00:15:34.780
Don't let it get away!
Fire! Fire! Fire!

00:15:40.250 --> 00:15:41.460
Got her!

00:15:49.420 --> 00:15:51.470
Target sunk!

00:15:51.470 --> 00:15:52.630
Good riddance!

00:15:56.640 --> 00:15:58.850
Depth, 150 meters.

00:15:59.100 --> 00:16:00.810
Water leaks all over starboard side.

00:16:00.810 --> 00:16:03.520
Man the starboard pumps at once!

00:16:12.780 --> 00:16:15.410
We've hit bottom. Depth, 200 meters.

00:16:15.410 --> 00:16:17.620
Drain the crude oil from tanks
numbers three through six.

00:16:17.620 --> 00:16:19.830
Eject all materials contained
in the aft hangar.

00:16:19.830 --> 00:16:21.290
They have to think they've sunk us.

00:16:21.290 --> 00:16:22.250
Understood.

00:16:27.130 --> 00:16:30.010
Materials and crude have been ejected.

00:16:30.010 --> 00:16:32.220
All quarters begin making
emergency repairs.

00:16:32.220 --> 00:16:32.670
Aye, Sir.

00:16:32.670 --> 00:16:37.140
We now have only enough power
to surface one more time.

00:16:37.140 --> 00:16:42.100
All we can do now is hope that the
fleet believes we've sunk and leaves.

00:16:45.810 --> 00:16:49.110
Captain, they weren't as
tough as we thought.

00:16:49.530 --> 00:16:51.610
We can't jump to conclusions.

00:16:51.610 --> 00:16:55.610
We'll wait a while and make sure.
That ship is really a monster.

00:16:55.610 --> 00:16:59.450
That was a fighting submarine
at least 150 meters long.

00:16:59.450 --> 00:17:02.080
I wonder what country it belongs to?

00:17:02.080 --> 00:17:07.920
That doesn't matter. It has murdered
thousands of men at sea.

00:17:08.290 --> 00:17:10.380
It deserves to be sunk!

00:17:15.970 --> 00:17:17.760
We'd better get out of here!

00:17:20.140 --> 00:17:23.140
Lethal gas in Second Auxiliary
Engine Room!

00:17:29.310 --> 00:17:32.190
Seal off the Auxiliary Engine Room.

00:17:32.190 --> 00:17:35.530
But Fait and two others are
still in that room!

00:17:37.110 --> 00:17:38.120
Seal it off!

00:17:38.120 --> 00:17:39.580
Captain Nemo!

00:17:40.330 --> 00:17:42.580
I'll go and get them out!

00:17:42.580 --> 00:17:43.700
I'll go too!

00:17:43.700 --> 00:17:44.330
Jean!

00:17:46.790 --> 00:17:48.330
Mr. Fait...

00:17:53.420 --> 00:17:55.420
It's no use! It won't open!

00:18:13.190 --> 00:18:15.780
It's no use! There are
no more hatches!

00:18:17.200 --> 00:18:18.360
Mr. Fait!

00:18:19.320 --> 00:18:20.030
I know!

00:18:21.780 --> 00:18:25.750
Chief Engineer, please
open this bulkhead!

00:18:25.750 --> 00:18:28.080
Hurry or Mr. Fait will die!

00:18:28.080 --> 00:18:33.590
I can't! If I open it, the poison
gas will get you!

00:18:34.210 --> 00:18:35.670
Oh, no.

00:18:36.210 --> 00:18:41.600
Isn't this ship full of futuristic science?!

00:18:41.600 --> 00:18:43.850
Please save Mr. Fait!

00:18:43.850 --> 00:18:48.390
This ship is made up of super science,
but it cannot work miracles.

00:18:48.390 --> 00:18:50.900
There's nothing we can do!

00:18:52.650 --> 00:18:55.400
No! We can't just stand by
and watch them die!

00:18:55.900 --> 00:18:57.650
Can't you do something?!

00:18:57.650 --> 00:19:00.700
If we surface and purge off the gas,
they can be saved,

00:19:00.700 --> 00:19:04.370
but we cannot surface now. I'm sorry.

00:19:08.370 --> 00:19:12.420
That's right. If we surface, that
warship will destroy us.

00:19:13.000 --> 00:19:14.540
Mr. Fait!

00:19:14.540 --> 00:19:16.710
Jean, is that you?

00:19:16.710 --> 00:19:18.380
Don't worry. We'll get you out.

00:19:18.380 --> 00:19:22.680
That's all right, Jean. If you try to
do that, you'll be killed too.

00:19:22.930 --> 00:19:26.720
No, I don't care about that!

00:19:26.720 --> 00:19:29.690
The Captain's decision is right.

00:19:29.690 --> 00:19:35.190
If he hadn't closed the bulwark, the
engine room would be full of gas.

00:19:35.190 --> 00:19:36.940
It's better for a few to die than many.

00:19:37.440 --> 00:19:39.070
This is fate.

00:19:39.070 --> 00:19:40.150
It's not right!

00:19:40.150 --> 00:19:41.780
This is too cruel!

00:19:43.620 --> 00:19:47.990
Please, Captain Nemo! Please surface
and save Mr. Fait's life!

00:19:49.450 --> 00:19:54.380
Why won't you surface?! What's so
important about this ship's secrets?

00:19:54.380 --> 00:19:57.590
Wave a white flag, and everyone will
be saved! The warships won't fire!

00:19:57.590 --> 00:19:59.380
Everyone will be saved!

00:20:00.050 --> 00:20:03.760
Why do you have to kill again?!
They're your shipmates!

00:20:03.760 --> 00:20:06.470
You murderer! You're not human!

00:20:10.640 --> 00:20:15.110
Don't say another word! Can't you see
Captain Nemo is suffering the most?!

00:20:26.660 --> 00:20:28.120
Nadia...

00:20:28.990 --> 00:20:32.120
The science on board this ship is
beyond the man's present knowledge.

00:20:32.120 --> 00:20:34.790
It must not be seen.

00:20:35.500 --> 00:20:36.840
But...

00:20:36.840 --> 00:20:42.510
Please understand, Nadia. Don't say
anything bad about Captain Nemo.

00:20:43.130 --> 00:20:46.850
He's the only reason I'm on this ship.

00:20:48.140 --> 00:20:55.520
Captain Nemo, please complete this
ship's mission to destroy Neo Atlantis.

00:20:56.520 --> 00:20:57.900
Please...

00:20:58.980 --> 00:21:03.490
Jean, take care of yourself, and
take care of Nadia too.

00:21:03.490 --> 00:21:06.070
Just give her my flowers, and
you'll reach her heart.

00:21:06.070 --> 00:21:07.700
Mr. Fait!

00:21:08.490 --> 00:21:10.080
Well, so long.

00:21:26.640 --> 00:21:30.180
No! I don't want to die yet!

00:21:30.180 --> 00:21:33.480
There are so many things
I still want to do!

00:21:33.480 --> 00:21:34.810
I don't want to...

00:21:34.810 --> 00:21:39.690
Mr. Fait! Mr. Fait! Mr. Fait! Mr. Fait!

00:21:39.690 --> 00:21:43.610
Mr. Fait! Mr. Fait! Mr. Fait!

00:21:44.110 --> 00:21:47.070
Mr. Fait... Mr. Fait...

00:21:48.620 --> 00:21:49.530
Mr. Fait!

00:22:22.650 --> 00:22:24.990
All disrupting materials have
been demagnetized.

00:22:24.990 --> 00:22:27.450
All sonar detectors are
back in operation.

00:22:28.200 --> 00:22:30.740
There are no objects on the
surface or in the sea.

00:22:30.740 --> 00:22:33.160
The American Fleet has departed.

00:22:34.910 --> 00:22:37.750
Okay. Ascend to the surface.

00:22:37.750 --> 00:22:39.080
Aye, Sir.

00:23:01.770 --> 00:23:06.230
Mr. Fait, these are your flowers.
We want to return them to you.

00:23:16.950 --> 00:23:19.120
What a cold group!

00:23:19.540 --> 00:23:21.830
Don't they have any feelings
for their dead?

00:23:22.670 --> 00:23:25.090
No time for tears, I guess.

00:23:25.090 --> 00:23:25.920
That's right!

00:23:25.920 --> 00:23:29.170
This ship is concerned only with
their war against Neo Atlantis.

00:23:31.720 --> 00:23:33.720
The only thing that matters
is killing each other off!
